      "problem": "Find $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\sqrt{\\pi}/2}\\tan\\left(2x^2-\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right).$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=\\dfrac{\\sqrt \\pi}{2}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\sqrt{\\pi }/2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2{x}^{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2{(\\frac{\\sqrt{\\pi }}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
